  "title": "Tests: Start removing the Python unittest dependency",
  "description": "The dependency on unittest is a holdover that prevents us from having a simpler test suite and taking advantage of the full feature set of pytest.\n\nReference from the pytest [documentation](https://docs.pytest.org/en/7.1.x/how-to/unittest.html):\n\n>>>\npytest supports running Python unittest-based tests out of the box. It’s meant for leveraging existing unittest-based test suites to use pytest as a test runner and also allow to incrementally adapt the test suite to take full advantage of pytest’s features.\n>>>\n\nHaving some unittest compatibility is useful to start using Pytest. This MR is the second step to that, to remove legacy code.\n\nStart small with the suite_capture test module.",
